Article 9
Sexual violence as referred to in Article 6 letter c is caused by:
a. acts constituting sexual harassment;
b. forced sexual intercourse;
c. forced sexual intercourse in an unnatural or unwanted manner; and/or
d. forced sexual intercourse with another person for commercial purposes and/or specific purposes.

Article 5
The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:
a. forms of Violence;
b. rights of Victims;
c. obligations and responsibilities;
d. implementation of protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence;
e. coordination and cooperation;
f. participation of the Community and business sector;
g. guidance and supervision;
h. reporting; and
i. sources of funding.

Article 16
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the Community as referred to in Article 13 letter b, shall be implemented in the form of Community participation.
(2) The form of Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:
   a. establishing family partners at the Kelurahan/Village level;
   b. establishing women and children protection units within community organizations;
   c. conducting independent socialization of the rights of Women and Children;
   d. providing first aid to Victims; and
   e. reporting to the competent authorities if Violence against Victims occurs in their environment.
(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, private sector, and mass media.
(4) The form of Community participation as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be implemented responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

