CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 12
Every Victim has the right to obtain:
a. protection;
b. information;
c. health services in accordance with medical needs;
d. continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage;
e. special handling related to the confidentiality of the Victim;
f. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations;
g. guarantee of rights related to status as a Family member as well as a member of the Community; and
h. spiritual guidance services.

Article 41
(1) In certain circumstances, the Regional Government may cooperate with: a. other regional governments;
b. the police;
c. advocates;
d. health workers;
e. social workers;
f. assistant/companion volunteers;
g. spiritual advisers;
h. other law enforcers;
i. the National Commission on Violence against Women;
j. the Indonesian Child Protection Commission or Child Protection Institutions; and/or
k. certain parties desired for the benefit of the Victim,
to assist the Victim in the process at court hearings.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of: a. socialization;
b. provision of legal aid;
c. health services;
d. assistance to the Victim;
e. counseling;
f. social rehabilitation;
g. spiritual guidance; and/or
h. return and social reintegration.

Article 25
The Implementation of Services and assistance to Victims, is carried out with the principles of:
a. fast, safe, and empathetic;
b. guarantee of confidentiality;
c. easily accessible; and
d. free of charge.

Article 5
The scope of this Regional Regulation includes:
a. forms of Violence;
b. rights of Victims;
c. obligations and responsibilities;
d. implementation of protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence;
e. coordination and cooperation;
f. participation of the Community and business sector;
g. guidance and supervision;
h. reporting; and
i. sources of funding.

Article 22
(1) Prevention of the occurrence of Violence against Women and Children as referred to in Article 21, shall be implemented by Regional apparatus whose duties and functions are in the field of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. Women’s Empowerment and Child Protection;
f. mental and spiritual; and
g. public tranquility and order.
(2) Prevention of Violence by Regional apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional action plan.
(3) Further provisions regarding the mechanism for implementing prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by a Regent Regulation.

Article 2
Protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence is implemented based on the principles of:
a. respect for Human Rights;
b. the right to life, survival, and development;
c. non-discrimination;
d. the best interests of the Child;
e. justice and Gender equality; and
f. protection of victims.

